Shared protocol test vectors.

Each file here pins one wire or file format that more than one program
implements. The tests of every implementation load the same file, so a change
on one side that the others do not follow fails a test instead of a session.

  aoa-frames.vectors     USB accessory link frames    Go host, Android app
  mux-frames.vectors     input-channel mux frames     Go host, Android app
  idd-ioctl.vectors      virtual display driver API   Go host, dd-host (and Public.h)
  display-claims.json    shared display claims file   Go host, dd-host
  desktop-status.json    dd-host status.json          dd-host writes, Go host reads

.vectors files hold one case per line: a name, then key=value pairs (hex in
lowercase, "-" for empty). Lines starting with # are comments. The format is
plain so that every language reads it without a JSON library.

To change a format: change the vectors first, then every implementation, and
describe the change in FUNCTIONALITY.md section 3.
